    "Explicit conversion validates all inputs before mutation, preserves every execution field and raw byte, pins original/replacement snapshots, refuses protected/foreign/plain/archive sources, rejects committed and working destination collisions, enforces original-envelope digest filenames, and retires source envelopes and payloads only with complete reference accounting.",
    "All-parent map-admission collision checks, transient mutation and deletion checks, immutable maps and both map sides, global inherited-owner source verification, raw-storage alias classification and narrow exact bound binary-payload proofs are fail-closed.",
    "Retained-base compatibility proves pre-import byte-exact original admission, unique recorded merge-base, source still unmerged, unused protected-path base-advance history and original-prefix audit. Every actual-base descendant containing source must contain original admission. Fresh conversion retains actual-base-to-source ancestry.",
    "Generic availability fallback applies only to an absent current path at the exact recorded reviewed revision. Present invalid artifacts/parents and unavailable historical sources remain rejected. Selected review/result/freshness and command/tested/exit binding functions retain their exact revision rules.",
    "Conversion cannot use tested/review bookkeeping suffixes. Exact tested-to-result suffix passes and adds only own result/evidence bookkeeping. Representation changes precede tested implementation.",
    "Frozen Protocol/DB, requirement set and HG051 archival authority remain unchanged. Scope includes no runtime, DB, provider, CI, credentials, installer or unrelated task changes. Current index changes are derived hashes; manifest changes are own append/derived rows."
  ],
